WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.164
A widget in a layer appears on a page only when the rule

00:00:04.164 --> 00:00:05.593
of that layer is true.

00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:09.421
This video shows the conditions a rule can hold, how to combine them,

00:00:09.421 --> 00:00:11.820
and how to check the result on your site.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.336
Each widget on the Widgets and Layers page belongs to a layer, and

00:00:20.336 --> 00:00:21.968
each layer has one rule.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:25.667
Each time the site displays a page, it checks the rule of each

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.244
layer that has widgets.

00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:30.290
If the rule is true, its published widgets appear.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.357
A rule is a list of conditions, and every condition in the list

00:00:35.357 --> 00:00:38.047
must be true for the rule to be true.

00:00:38.047 --> 00:00:43.740
A rule without conditions is never true, so a layer without conditions shows nothing.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.183
Some conditions look at the page.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:54.613
Homepage tests for the home page, Url compares the path of the address,

00:00:54.613 --> 00:01:00.250
Content type compares the type of content on show, and Culture compares the current culture.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.013
Others look at the visitor.

00:01:03.013 --> 00:01:07.709
Is authenticated is true for a signed-in user, Is anonymous is true for

00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:12.710
everyone else, and Role compares the roles of the user with a name you type.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.804
Boolean is fixed to true or false, so a Boolean set to true

00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:19.675
is true on every page.

00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:24.754
Javascript runs a script that must return true or false, for cases the

00:01:24.754 --> 00:01:27.160
other conditions do not cover.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.445
Two conditions are groups that hold other conditions.

00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:35.518
All is true when every condition inside it is true, and Any is

00:01:35.518 --> 00:01:38.214
true when at least one of them is true.

00:01:38.214 --> 00:01:41.090
A group with nothing inside is never true.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.454
Url, Content type, Culture and Role compare with an operation:

00:01:46.454 --> 00:01:51.679
Equals, Starts with, Ends with, Contains, or the Does not form of each.

00:01:51.679 --> 00:01:54.800
Comparisons ignore upper and lower case.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.253
Open the Design menu, then Widgets.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:06.295
The Widgets and Layers page shows the zones with their widgets, and the list of layers.

00:02:06.295 --> 00:02:10.360
Let's edit the Welcome layer, which has one widget and no conditions.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.906
Select Edit.

00:02:11.906 --> 00:02:16.716
The Rules section is empty, and the page asks for at least one condition.

00:02:16.716 --> 00:02:20.674
Until you add one, the rule is never true, so the widget of

00:02:20.674 --> 00:02:23.170
this layer is hidden on every page.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:30.135
Select Add above the list of conditions.

00:02:30.135 --> 00:02:34.834
The Available Rules dialog shows every condition as a card, and the Filter

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.419
box narrows the list.

00:02:36.419 --> 00:02:41.353
The layer should show on two different pages, so let's find the Any condition.

00:02:41.814 --> 00:02:44.476
Select Add on the Any condition card.

00:02:44.476 --> 00:02:49.491
Name the group Home or About, so the rule reads clearly, and select Create.

00:02:49.491 --> 00:02:53.144
The group joins the rule, and it holds no conditions.

00:02:57.338 --> 00:03:01.165
Select Add on the group itself, not the one above the list, so

00:03:01.165 --> 00:03:03.979
the condition you add goes inside the group.

00:03:03.979 --> 00:03:08.088
Filter for homepage, and select Add on the Homepage condition card.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:12.088
The editor offers Is homepage and Is not homepage.

00:03:12.088 --> 00:03:17.074
Is homepage is already selected, which is what we need, so select Create.

00:03:17.533 --> 00:03:21.572
Select Add on the group again, and choose the Url condition card.

00:03:21.572 --> 00:03:24.473
Its editor asks for an operation and a value.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:30.799
Choose Starts with as the operation, type /about as the value, and select Create.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:36.120
The condition is true for any page whose address path begins with /about.

00:03:36.607 --> 00:03:41.287
The group lists both conditions, and it needs only one of them to be true.

00:03:45.527 --> 00:03:47.109
Let's look at the site.

00:03:47.109 --> 00:03:51.966
Each condition was saved when we selected Create, so the layer needs no other save.

00:03:51.966 --> 00:03:57.477
On the home page, the Welcome note appears, because the home page meets the Homepage condition.

00:03:57.943 --> 00:03:59.808
Select About in the menu.

00:03:59.808 --> 00:04:04.923
The note appears here too, because the address of this page starts with /about.

00:04:05.402 --> 00:04:07.328
Open one of the blog posts.

00:04:07.328 --> 00:04:11.940
Its address matches neither condition, so the group is false, the rule is

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.042
false, and the note is hidden.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:22.052
Back in the layer, select Add above the list of conditions.

00:04:22.052 --> 00:04:27.597
This time, choose the Is authenticated condition card, which is true for signed-in users.

00:04:28.073 --> 00:04:31.338
This condition has no settings, so select Create.

00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:34.603
It is added to the rule itself, beside the group.

00:04:35.057 --> 00:04:38.697
Conditions placed directly in the rule must all be true.

00:04:38.697 --> 00:04:43.041
The group must match and the visitor must be signed in, so anonymous

00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:45.037
visitors never see the note.

00:04:49.237 --> 00:04:52.270
Each condition has an Edit button and a Delete button.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.658
You can also drag a condition by its row to change its order,

00:04:55.658 --> 00:04:59.197
or to move it into another group that already holds a condition.

00:04:59.947 --> 00:05:04.716
The Content type condition only knows about content that the page shows in full.

00:05:04.716 --> 00:05:08.487
It ignores widgets, so it cannot test the content of a widget.

00:05:09.237 --> 00:05:14.977
To change rules, a user needs the Manage layers permission, which administrators have by default.

00:05:15.727 --> 00:05:18.619
The Rules module has no screen of its own.

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:23.740
Enabling Layers in Tools, Features enables Rules with it, and the Layers module

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.427
shows the rule editor.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:30.676
A rule is a list of conditions that must all be true, and

00:05:30.676 --> 00:05:33.049
the All and Any groups let you mix them.

00:05:33.049 --> 00:05:36.866
Build rules on the edit page of a layer, and check them on the site.

00:05:36.866 --> 00:05:38.207
Thanks for watching.

